A||N||7||MikeSchaefer||Seat Backs Interchangable (drivers/pass)?||||5||
Z||000000||MikeSchaefer||09-21-2000||02:03 AM||||Hey,<BR>My girlfriend's 86 has the legendary driver's side rip developing.  We fixed it once, but it is back.  Is there a place I can get the factory cloth to fix it with?  Or could I swap the entire back with a passenger side seatback out of another gray interior Fiero?<BR>Thanks,<BR>Michael Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||09-21-2000||02:15 AM||||The seat backs are interchangable. But just the cover not the entire back assembly. So if you know of a good passenger seat you can swap the skins.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||09-21-2000||02:50 AM||||I have done the passenger seat back cover to drivers side swap once and will be doing it again (different car).  Doesn't take too long nor is it overly difficult.  I never pass up a good passenger seat cover at the u-pull-it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||09-21-2000||05:23 AM||||Not doubting you, Dave, but I thought the entire seat backs were interchangable.  What part is backwards and could it be easily modified?  370,000 good pass seatbacks out there and only 4 good drivers side seatbacks.  There's gotta be something we can do to make it work.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MikeSchaefer||09-21-2000||11:38 AM||||Hi, Does anyone have a good skin for sale? <BR>Thanks for the responses,<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000005||theogre||09-21-2000||07:31 PM||||the backs I've seen all have the bar that the pivot blot goes thru welded to the framing. That bar is why you can't trade them.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||09-21-2000||11:18 PM||||The hinge points on the seat backs are made differently. One side is formed to hold the coil spring and lever assembly the other side is just a hinge point.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cooter||09-21-2000||11:28 PM||||On my last seat cover swap, I used passenger covers for the drivers seat and about halfway through, I ran out of hog-rings. I just used a few zip-ties and it looked great when all was done.||||reg||1
